# No Cursor co-author on commits

**STRICT — never break this.**

When creating git commits:

1. **Do NOT** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any Cursor / cursoragent co-author trailer).
2. **Do NOT** add any other AI/tool co-author trailer unless the user explicitly asks.
3. Commit message body must be only the user's intended message (subject + optional body). No agent branding.
4. If the environment tries to inject a Cursor co-author into the commit command, strip it before running `git commit`. Never paste those trailers into the HEREDOC.
5. Author/committer must remain the user's normal git identity (`git config user.name` / `user.email`) — never change git config to Cursor.
6. After `git commit`, if `git log -1 --format=%B` shows a Cursor `Co-authored-by` line and the commit has **not** been pushed, amend with the same message without that trailer (only when amend rules otherwise allow). If already pushed, tell the user and do not rewrite history unless they ask.
7. Repo safety net: `.githooks/prepare-commit-msg` strips these trailers — keep `core.hooksPath=.githooks` set for this repo.
